%U A398578 11834,12035,12090,13880,13924,14408,14496,14980,15024,17598,17642,18170,19955,20010
%N A398578 Base-12 happy numbers.
%H A398578 Derek Israel White, <a href="/A398578/b398578.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398578 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Happy_number">Happy number</a>.
%e A398578 680 = 488_12, 4^2+8^2+8^2 = 144 = 100_12, 1^2 = 1, thus 680 is a happy number in base 12.
%t A398578 happyQ[k_, b_] := NestWhile[Total[IntegerDigits[#, b]^2] &, k, UnsameQ, All] == 1; Select[Range[22500], happyQ[#, 12] &] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 03 2026 *)
%o A398578 (Python)
%o A398578 from sympy.ntheory import digits
%o A398578 def ok(n, b=12): # n is happy in base b
%o A398578     seen = set()
%o A398578     while n not in seen:
%o A398578         seen.add(n)
%o A398578         n = sum(d**2 for d in digits(n, b)[1:])
%o A398578     return n==1
%o A398578 print([k for k in range(20011) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Aug 03 2026
